   691	\[
   692	N^2-\|\mathbf Z(\mathfrak c)\|^2
   693	\le C(\alpha\beta)^2.                                \tag{7.5}
   694	\]
   695	
   696	Any proof must use more than the support of the critical divisor: it must
   697	use the exact Keller multiplicities and their transforms at every boundary
   698	breakpoint.
   699	
   700	### Status ledger
   701	
   702	| Statement | Status |
   703	|---|---|
   704	| balanced rooftop is canonical | **EXACT** |
   705	| rooftop energy equals `td/(alpha beta)` | **EXACT** |
   706	| energy equals `Sum a_P b_P/nu_P` | **EXACT**, using `TDBOUND.md` |
   707	| Hodge / mixed-volume inequality gives the unit bound | **NO; wrong direction** |
   708	| ADE support alone gives `Delta^2 >= -2` | **NO; the residual class must separately be a root** |
   709	| projective Jacobian identities (4.1)--(4.2) | **EXACT** |
   710	| ordinary log-ramification effectivity gives a degree ceiling | **NO immediate implication; line class cancels in the natural log pair** |
   711	| normalized multi-Rees finite generation gives per-pair finite energy | **EXACT** |
   712	| finite generation gives a `B`-uniform finite bound | **NO; refuted without Keller by (5.5)** |
   713	| any `B`-independent `C` for Keller pairs | **CONJECTURE KJN(C) / G5-RBE(C)** |
   714	| sharp unit bound | **CONJECTURE KJN(1)** |
   715	
   716	## 8. Final conclusion
   717	
   718	The rooftop construction has done all the canonicalization one can ask of
   719	it. It replaces packet concentration and computes the whole G5 defect on a
   720	single normalized three-generated ideal. But its convexity is bookkeeping,
   721	not coercivity.
   722	
   723	The sharp obstruction can now be stated without ambiguity:
   724	
   725	\[
   726	\boxed{
   727	\text{prove that the pure-boundary Jacobian identity (4.1), after base
   728	resolution, forces a uniform Green-capacity bound (6.3).}}
   729	\]
   730	
   731	Hodge index proves the opposite-side inequality. Log-Calabi--Yau
   732	ramification cancels the line class. Finite generation is only pointwise,
   733	and explicit common-leading-power controls have energy
   734	`B^2-B/beta`. Therefore neither the unit bound nor any cofinal weak finite
   735	bound is presently proved.
   736	
   737	The honest final label is:
   738	
   739	\[
   740	\boxed{
   741	\textbf{OBSTRUCTED: exact reduction to CONJECTURE KJN(C); no uniform }C
   742	\textbf{ obtained.}}
   743	\]

